<description>
Paint a teal diamond envelope around each straight foreground bar.

Input structure
- The grid has a single background color and one non-background foreground color.
- Every foreground object is a solid horizontal or vertical one-cell-thick bar.
- Teal is absent from the input and is reserved for the added envelope pixels.

Rule
- Keep every original foreground bar unchanged.
- For a horizontal bar, paint teal rows above and below it; each step away from the bar shortens the interval by one pixel at both ends.
- For a vertical bar, apply the same shrinking construction rotated ninety degrees.

Key insight
- A bar of length L defines a centered diamond of radius floor((L - 1) / 2), with the original bar forming the middle line and teal filling only the surrounding background cells.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "solid horizontal or vertical one-cell-thick foreground bars on a background",
  "transform": "around each bar, paint background pixels teal in the centered diamond envelope: each step away from the bar shortens the interval by one pixel from both ends; preserve the original bars"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 17-22 rows x 19-22 cols
  background: BLACK [observed]; any color except TEAL allowed
  bar_color: single non-bg foreground color; RED [observed]; must not be TEAL
  teal: absent from input; used only in output for diamond envelopes
  bars:
    count: 1-3
    shape: solid 1-cell-thick horizontal or vertical segments
    length: 5-14 (radius = floor((L-1)/2) >= 1, so length >= 3 required)
    orientation: mix of H and V allowed
  diamond_envelope:
    rule: |
      For each bar of length L, centered diamond with radius R = floor((L-1)/2).
      Each row/col offset d (1..R) from bar paints teal on the sub-segment
      shortened by d pixels from both ends, on both sides of the bar.
    clearance: every bar must have >= radius cells of free space in all 4 cardinal directions from its bounding box
    no_overlap: diamonds must not overlap each other or any bar pixels
  output: same grid with teal diamond envelopes painted on background cells around each bar

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size in 17-22 x 19-22.
    2. Pick bar count (1-3) and for each bar choose orientation (H/V) and length (5-14).
    3. Compute radius R = floor((L-1)/2) for each bar.
    4. Place bars one at a time ensuring (a) bar + R-radius clearance to all grid edges,
       (b) full diamond bounding box (2R+1 x L for H, L x 2R+1 for V) does not overlap
       any previously placed bar or its diamond bounding box.
    5. Build output by painting teal diamond envelopes around each bar on the bg grid.
    6. Input is the grid with only the bars (no teal).
```
